flowchart TB
    accTitle: The path of a request through the Worker
    accDescr: Telegram calls the Worker at /telegram with a button or a text of the maintainer, the GitHub App at /github with an event, and the control repository at /control with an answer. src/index.ts turns away every other path and method. An event of GitHub is checked in the Worker itself, by screen() of src/routes.ts: its signature first, then the rules of rules.ts, and an event that means nothing is answered there, without Workers KV and without the Durable Object. The rest goes to Serial, the one Durable Object of src/serial.ts, which runs one change at a time, as it does with the run of the schedule every 15 minutes. routes.ts checks where a request of Telegram or of the control repository comes from, by the secret header of Telegram or the signature of the control repository, and refuses it without a change otherwise. updates.ts, rules.ts, control.ts and schedule.ts decide what it means, and pager.ts and actions.ts apply it: the state of the things in Workers KV, through store.ts, one message per thing in Telegram, through render.ts, texts.ts and telegram.ts, and the action of a button on GitHub, through github.ts.

    telegram["`**Telegram** at /telegram: a button or a text of the maintainer`"]
    github["`**The GitHub App** at /github: an event`"]
    control["`**The control repository** at /control: an answer`"]
    cron["`**The schedule** of Cloudflare, every 15 minutes`"]
    index["`**src/index.ts** turns away every other path and method`"]
    screen{"`**screen() of routes.ts**, in the Worker: is the event signed, and does a rule of rules.ts want it?`"}
    answered["`No: answered at once, without Workers KV and the Durable Object`"]
    serial["`**Serial**, the one Durable Object of src/serial.ts, runs one change at a time`"]
    routes{"`**routes.ts**: does it prove its origin?`"}
    refused["`No: refused, and nothing changes`"]
    doors["`**updates.ts, rules.ts, control.ts** and **schedule.ts** decide what it means`"]
    apply["`**pager.ts** and **actions.ts** apply it`"]
    kv["`**Workers KV**, through store.ts: the state of each thing`"]
    message["`**Telegram**, through render.ts, texts.ts and telegram.ts: one message per thing, edited in place`"]
    act["`**GitHub**, through github.ts: the action of a button`"]

    telegram --> index
    github --> index
    control --> index
    index -- "an event of GitHub" --> screen
    screen --> answered
    screen -- "yes: its signal" --> serial
    index -- "Telegram and the control repository" --> serial
    cron --> serial
    serial -- "a request" --> routes
    serial -- "a run of the schedule" --> doors
    routes --> refused
    routes -- "yes" --> doors
    doors --> apply
    apply --> kv
    apply --> message
    apply --> act

    classDef you fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class telegram you
    class github,control,cron,index,screen,serial,routes,doors,apply bot
    class refused,answered,kv,message,act done
